---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import InstallCommandTabs from "../components/InstallCommandTabs/InstallCommandTabs.astro";
import "./_install/install.scss";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Install"
  pageTitle="Crona install guide"
  description="Install Crona with Homebrew on macOS and Linux, Scoop on Windows, or source builds for advanced local setups."
>
  <section class="container section">
    <div class="page-header flow measure">
      <p class="eyebrow">Install</p>
      <h1>Install Crona the managed way</h1>
      <p>
        Homebrew is the managed path on macOS and Linux.
        Scoop is the managed path on Windows.
        `go install` remains the advanced source path.
        GitHub Releases are the canonical binary source, and the legacy install scripts stay pinned at `v1.6.0` for migration off older installs.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-body flow">
      <div class="install-hub">
        <InstallCommandTabs />
      </div>

      <div class="install-handoff">
        <a class="install-handoff__card" href="/docs/migration/">
          <span>Migration</span>
          <strong>Switch install methods safely</strong>
          <p>Back up, clear the old runtime, reinstall with the package manager you want to keep, and restore.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="install-handoff__card" href="/docs/install/">
          <span>Reference</span>
          <strong>Read the full install guide</strong>
          <p>See runtime paths, release channels, update behavior, and notification sound attribution in one place.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="install-handoff__card" href="/docs/migration/legacy-to-brew/">
          <span>Homebrew</span>
          <strong>Legacy to Homebrew</strong>
          <p>Use the macOS and Linux migration guide when you are moving off the legacy script.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="install-handoff__card" href="/docs/migration/legacy-to-go/">
          <span>Source install</span>
          <strong>Legacy to Go</strong>
          <p>Keep the source-install flow with `go install` after you migrate away from the script.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="install-handoff__card" href="/docs/migration/legacy-to-scoop/">
          <span>Windows</span>
          <strong>Legacy to Scoop</strong>
          <p>Move a script-based Windows install onto the managed Scoop path without losing local state.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
